Title: The Lighthouse Keeper
Credit: Written by
Author: Test Fixture

FADE IN:

EXT. HARBOUR - DAY

Gulls wheel over a grey harbour. MARA (40s) hauls a crate onto the jetty.

MARA
Tide's turning. We go tonight.

TOM (O.S.)
Not without the lamp oil.

INT. LIGHTHOUSE - NIGHT

The lamp room. TOM (60s) trims a wick.

TOM
She'll not see the rocks without it.

MARA
Then we light it.

CUT TO:

EXT. CLIFF PATH - DAWN

Mara climbs alone.

INT./EXT. HARBOUR MASTER'S OFFICE - CONTINUOUS

ELSIE (30s) watches through the glass.

ELSIE
(into radio)
Keeper, do you copy?

TOM (V.O.)
I copy.

FADE OUT.
